Z||000001||bHooper||11-21-2000||11:18 PM||||Ouch!  Thats a lot of moola!  I just spent $63 on rear calipers (new from Autozone) and $40 on rear rotors (used from Fieroshop), plus $15 on pads.  The fronts cant be that much more, even with the combo rotor hub. <P>As for a cheap altenator, I got mine for about $64 at Advance Auto!<P>Don't froget to keep the heat shield off of yours!<P>good luck!<BR>hoop||||reg||1
Z||000002||Tom88gt||11-21-2000||11:19 PM||||rebuild it yourself.  Kits are about $10-15.  Available at any autoparts store.  They work and work well.||||reg||3
Z||000003||terryk||11-22-2000||01:25 AM||||Unless the alternator is making noises (bearing), the regulator or diodes might just be dead. You can get a brush/reg/diode kit pretty cheap.<P>Otherwise, buy the most expensive alternator you can find. Otherwise you'll just keep putting them it. A GM reman is your best bet.<BR>||||reg||1
